--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
> Hello @krekken & @maldarol
> 
> Could you please provide clear and concise steps to reproduce the issue pray Please check and feedback.
> 
> Thanks!

i made a module, that reproduces the problem, but i'll describe what i did, in case you don't want to rely on that. 
https://github.com/krekken/ordererrorreproduce

So i installed the hook like this, in the main php file:

```php

    public function install()
    {
        Configuration::updateValue('ORDERERRORREPRODUCE_LIVE_MODE', false);

        return parent::install() &&
            $this->registerHook('header') &&
            $this->registerHook('displayAdminOrderMain') && //this is the hook
            $this->registerHook('backOfficeHeader');
    }
```
And then i made a form inside the hook. 
```php
    public function hookDisplayAdminOrderMain(array $params)
    {
        $task = new Task();
        $task->setTask('Write a blog post');
        $task->setDueDate(new \DateTime('tomorrow'));

        $formFactory = $this->get('form.factory');
        $form = $formFactory->createBuilder()
            ->add('task', TextType::class)
            ->add('dueDate', DateType::class)
            ->add('save', SubmitType::class, ['label' => 'Create Task'])
            ->getForm();

        $form->handleRequest($params['request']);

        return $this->render('@Modules/ordererrorreproduce/views/templates/admin/error.html.twig', [
            'form' => $form->createView(),
        ]);
    }
```
Entity of the form:
```php
<?php 
namespace OrderError\Form\Entity;

class Task
{
    protected $task;
    protected $dueDate;

    public function getTask(): string
    {
        return $this->task;
    }

    public function setTask(string $task): void
    {
        $this->task = $task;
    }

    public function getDueDate(): ?\DateTime
    {
        return $this->dueDate;
    }

    public function setDueDate(?\DateTime $dueDate): void
    {
        $this->dueDate = $dueDate;
    }
}
```

the twig:
```twig
{% block content %}
<div class="card">
    <div class="card-body">
        {{ form(form) }}
    </div>
</div>    
{% endblock %}
```

this module will work in 1.7.7.8, but will produce error in 1.7.8. the reason behind it, is that the request is missing from the $params array that the hook provides. Meaning, the issue is that the form here " $form->handleRequest($params['request']);", gets NULL, but in order to handle the form made with form.factory inside the hook, you need that request, but after the update from 1.7.7.8 to 1.7.8 that request object is missing.


-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------


1. Call the `displayAdminOrderMain` hook in `ps_qualityassurance` module while this hook display its params:
```
public function hookDisplayAdminOrderMain(array $params)
    {
          dump($params);
    }
```

2. BO > SELL > Orders > Edit an Order
3. Check the results below, it display the params
![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/23308427/140385070-ae7c0331-894a-4a2b-b559-177a514f99bf.png)

4. Upgrade your shop to 1.7.8.0
5. BO > SELL > Orders > Edit an Order
6. See error > some params are not displayed
![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/23308427/140385189-3a4ec3ba-8fb1-47b8-95fd-a53edbd17595.png)

**Screenshots**
The error in symfony profiler
![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/23308427/140385283-f4c56be7-b573-4e97-a855-f5b913886de8.png)

Steps to reproduce the behavior:

1. Develop a module to add a new column on backoffice Orders grid using actionOrderGridQueryBuilderModifier hook.
2. Add a new data column to Orders grid (similar to example for Customers grid from official doc: https://devdocs.prestashop.com/1.7/modules/sample-modules/grid-and-identifiable-object-form-hooks-usage/#extending-grid-query-builder)
2. Click on backoffice Orders menu
3. Use "New client" filter with any value (Yes or No) and click on Search button
4. An error 500 is shown due to and incorrect table alias

**Screenshots**

- Module hooks code:
![1](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/18466848/121567527-49093a00-c9e4-11eb-9d18-16fa920a64ad.JPG)
![2](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/18466848/121567547-4dcdee00-c9e4-11eb-9236-9edd66e36a34.JPG)

hookActionOrderGridDefinitionModifier code:
```
public function hookActionOrderGridDefinitionModifier(array $params)
{
    $definition = $params['definition'];

    $definition->getColumns()->addAfter(
        'date_add',
        (new BooleanColumn('from_app'))
            ->setName($this->l('App order'))
            ->setOptions([
                'field' => 'from_app',
                'true_name' => $this->trans('Yes', [], 'Admin.Global'),
                'false_name' => $this->trans('No', [], 'Admin.Global'),
                'clickable' => true,
            ])
    );

    $definition->getFilters()->add(
        (new Filter('from_app', YesAndNoChoiceType::class))
        ->setTypeOptions([
            'required' => false,
        ])    
        ->setAssociatedColumn('from_app')
    );
}

public function hookActionOrderGridQueryBuilderModifier(array $params)
{
    $searchQueryBuilder = $params['search_query_builder'];

    $searchCriteria = $params['search_criteria'];

    $searchQueryBuilder->addSelect(
        'app.`id_order` IS NOT NULL AS `from_app`'
    );

    $searchQueryBuilder->leftJoin(
        'o',
        '`app_order_table`',
        'app',
        'app.`id_order` = o.`id_order`'
    );

    if ('from_app' === $searchCriteria->getOrderBy()) {
        $searchQueryBuilder->orderBy('app.`id_order`', $searchCriteria->getOrderWay());
    }

    foreach ($searchCriteria->getFilters() as $filterName => $filterValue) {
        if ('from_app' === $filterName) {
            $searchQueryBuilder->andWhere('app.`id_order` IS ' . ($filterValue ? 'NOT' : '') . ' NULL');
        }
    }
}
```
- Error details:
![3](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/18466848/121567574-58888300-c9e4-11eb-848c-f746a80b4062.JPG)

ticket.bug:
Since this PR was merged https://github.com/PrestaShop/PrestaShop/pull/26748

The previous code was:
```php
    public static function getHookStatusByName($hook_name): bool
    {
        $sql = new DbQuery();
        $sql->select('active');
        $sql->from('hook', 'h');
        $sql->where('h.name = "' . pSQL($hook_name) . '"');

        return (bool) Db::getInstance()->getValue($sql);
    }
```

Now the code looks like this:

```php
    public static function getHookStatusByName($hook_name): bool
    {
        $hook_names = [];
        if (Cache::isStored('active_hooks')) {
            $hook_names = Cache::retrieve('active_hooks');
        } else {
            $sql = new DbQuery();
            $sql->select('name');
            $sql->from('hook', 'h');
            $sql->where('h.active = 1');
            $active_hooks = Db::getInstance()->executeS($sql);
            if (!empty($active_hooks)) {
                $hook_names = array_column($active_hooks, 'name');
                if (is_array($hook_names)) {
                    Cache::store('active_hooks', $hook_names);
                }
            }
        }

        return in_array($hook_name, $hook_names);
    }
```

The problem is that MySQL is not case sensitive, but `in_array` is.

So if for example in the BDD we have `ModuleRoutes` and in the code `moduleRoutes`
Or `displayOverrideTemplate` in the BDD but `DisplayOverrideTemplate` in the code

Then the hook doesn't trigger, before the modification it used to work.

When Prestashop is configured so that it does not use decimals, when validating the order with the 'validateOrder' method, the order is marked with payment error (PS_OS_ERROR)

on line 323 the error is thrown
```php
if ($order_status->logable && number_format($cart_total_paid, Context::getContext()->getComputingPrecision()) != number_format($amount_paid, _PS_PRICE_COMPUTE_PRECISION_)) {
    $id_order_state = Configuration::get('PS_OS_ERROR');
}
```

In the if, the amount is validated with the constant _PS_PRICE_COMPUTE_PRECISION_ and the configuration of the currency is not checked. In this case the variable **_$cart_total_paid_** always has a difference with the amount paid (**_number_format($amount_paid, _PS_PRICE_COMPUTE_PRECISION_)_**).

![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/36648048/140820904-b65822bc-b83f-408d-860b-94b7ed222edf.png)

